r or web view, add the session transfer token to the URL as a query","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter. Then your website can redirect the user to Auth0’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/authorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint, passing along the query","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter with the session transfer token. For example,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/example.com\/login?session_transfer_token=THE_TOKEN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re using ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKWebView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to open your website, you can place the session transfer token inside a cookie","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead. It will be automatically sent to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/authorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let cookie = HTTPCookie(properties: [","    .domain: \"YOUR_AUTH0_DOMAIN\", \/\/ Or custom domain, if your website is using one","    .path: \"\/\",","    .name: \"auth0_session_transfer_token\",","    .value: ssoCredentials.sessionTransferToken,","    .expires: ssoCredentials.expiresAt,","    .secure: true","])!","","webView.configuration.websiteDataStore.httpCookieStore.setCookie(cookie)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make sure the cookie’s domain matches the Auth0 domain your ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"website","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is using, regardless of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one your mobile app is using. Otherwise, the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/authorize"},{"text":" endpoint will not receive the cookie. If your website","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is using the provided Auth0 domain (like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","c